cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use benchsiDE, please cite it as below."
title: "benchsiDE: validated, client-side RNA-seq differential expression and discovery analysis"
version: 0.19.5-beta
date-released: "2026-09-25"
abstract: >-
  benchsiDE is a single-file web application for bulk RNA-seq analysis that runs
  entirely in the browser; expression data are not transmitted. It implements TMM
  normalization, filterByExpr filtering, moderated t, voom and covariate models,
  moderated F, gene-set testing (over-representation, preranked GSEA, CAMERA, FRY),
  module discovery and cross-dataset comparison. Each statistical routine is validated
  against its reference implementation (edgeR, limma, RRHO, RNASeqPower, scipy,
  statsmodels) by an in-browser self-test and by an external validation on a public
  dataset (GEO GSE63310).
authors:
  - family-names: "Yaron"
    given-names: "Jordan R."
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-4133-474X"
    affiliation: "Arizona State University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jyaron/benchsiDE"
url: "https://www.benchside.org"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - RNA-seq
  - differential expression
  - gene-set testing
  - client-side
  - limma
  - edgeR
  - reproducibility
